        <mxCell id="QcePuBtjHszSp8iwWYwL-118" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;Sequence of connection:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Phase 0 - Preconditions:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;P0. Client A has an active client_id/session_token from /register (kept alive via /heartbeat)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Phase 1 - Link Provisioning (Initiator):&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. Client A UI starts link session and creates rendezvous_id + secret (Local Crypto)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. Client A calls /connection/init via HTTPS&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. Gateway routes to Axum connection_init handler&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;4. Handler verifies client session token in SessionRegistry&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;5. Axum invokes RendezvousService to provision the connection&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;6. RendezvousService stores rendezvous token mapping in Redis&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;7. RendezvousService creates mailbox_meta in Redis + applies TTL&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;8. Server returns mailboxA + expires_at to Client A&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;9. Axum upgrades /ws subscription for mailboxA via WebSocket Endpoint&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;10. Client A shares token + secret out-of-band (deep link) to B&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Phase 2 - Join + Pairing (Responder):&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;11. Client B derives keys and calls /connection/join with token&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;12. RendezvousService consumes rendezvous token in Redis (GET then DEL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;13. RendezvousService creates mailboxB and pairs mailboxA&amp;lt;-&amp;gt;mailboxB&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;14. Axum triggers PushHub to emit a join marker event&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;15. PushHub routes fan-out event to WebSocket Endpoint&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;16. WebSocket Endpoint forwards join marker to Client A&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;17. Client B sends encrypted connect_request via /connection/send (ignored by A signaling parser)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Phase 3 - SDP/ICE Signaling Over Mailboxes:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;18. Client A accepts, WebRTC creates SDP offer, Local Crypto encrypts payload&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;19. Client A calls /connection/send to push encrypted offer + trickle ICE&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;20. WebSocket Endpoint forwards encrypted offer down to Client B via /ws push&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;21. Client B Signaling passes offer to B Crypto for decryption &amp;amp; payload processing&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;22. Client B generates SDP answer, encrypts, and calls /connection/send&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;23. WebSocket Endpoint forwards encrypted answer to Client A via /ws&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Phase 4 - Transport Establishment + Signaling Teardown:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;24. Client A ICE agent probes STUN and contributes to candidate pair nomination (TURN not configured here)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;25. Client B ICE agent probes STUN and contributes to candidate pair nomination&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;26. WebRTC PeerConnections establish DTLS handshake -&amp;gt; SRTP/SCTP up&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;27. Direct P2P data channels established; both clients close signaling mailboxes and move late control/ICE over data channels&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="340" width="610" x="1000" y="1910" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
